From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] zfs: make the ARC shrinker synchronous in hard mode so
 the reclaimer does not OOM while eviction is still in flight

OSv's memory reclaimer drives the ARC shrinker and, immediately after calling
it, checks whether any memory came back (reclaimer::_do_reclaim ->
wake_waiters); if none did it calls oom() and aborts the guest. The hard-mode
shrinker (osv_arc_lowmem) only calls arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink(), which
lowers arc_c and wakes the async arc_evict thread but returns immediately,
before any pages are actually freed. Under a burst (a large PostgreSQL
checkpoint stacking dirty buffers plus many backend allocations on top of the
ARC) the async eviction lags the allocation demand, so the reclaimer sees zero
freed bytes and OOMs even though eviction is in progress. This is the VU192
out-of-memory abort seen at high concurrency.

Add a synchronous variant, arc_reduce_target_size_shrink_sync(), that lowers
the target the same way and then blocks in arc_wait_for_eviction() until the
requested amount has actually been evicted (lax=B_TRUE so it returns early once
the ARC is no longer overflowing, and honoring arc_c_min so it cannot wait for
memory the ARC is not allowed to give up). The hard-mode shrinker now calls the
synchronous variant, so when the reclaimer is about to OOM the shrinker does
not return until real memory has come back; soft mode (osv_arc_sized_adjust)
stays asynchronous and unchanged. The waiter used by arc_wait_for_eviction is
already fork-COW-coherent (identity-heap, patch 0030), and the reclaimer thread
is allowed to block (it already blocks on _blocked.wait), so this is safe to
call from the shrinker context.

This is a generic ZFS-on-OSv memory-pressure fix: any workload that allocates
against a full ARC benefits from the shrinker actually freeing memory before
the reclaimer decides it cannot.

NOTE: the two hunks below are anchored on the arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink()
definition (module/zfs/arc.c) and the osv_arc_lowmem() body (zfs_initialize_osv.c) that
patch 0009 introduces. If the surrounding line numbers have drifted, apply with
`git apply --recount` (or `--3way`); the anchor text is unique in both files.
---
 module/os/osv/zfs/zfs_initialize_osv.c |  9 +++++++--
 module/zfs/arc.c                       | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/module/zfs/arc.c b/module/zfs/arc.c
--- a/module/zfs/arc.c
+++ b/module/zfs/arc.c
@@ -4799,6 +4799,31 @@ arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink(uint64_t to_free)
 	return (to_free);
 }
 
+/*
+ * OSv: synchronous hard-mode shrink.  Lower the target and kick eviction the
+ * same way arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink() does, then block until the
+ * requested amount has actually been evicted.  Called only from the hard-mode
+ * ARC shrinker (reclaimer about to OOM), so the caller wants real freed memory
+ * before it returns, not just a lowered target.  lax=B_TRUE returns early once
+ * the ARC stops overflowing; use_reserve=B_FALSE.  The waiter is fork-COW-
+ * coherent (identity heap, patch 0030); the OSv reclaimer thread may block.
+ */
+uint64_t
+arc_reduce_target_size_shrink_sync(uint64_t to_free)
+{
+	uint64_t asize_before = aggsum_value(&arc_sums.arcstat_size);
+	uint64_t requested = arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink(to_free);
+
+	if (requested == 0)
+		return (0);
+
+	arc_wait_for_eviction(requested, B_TRUE, B_FALSE);
+
+	uint64_t asize_after = aggsum_value(&arc_sums.arcstat_size);
+	return (asize_before > asize_after ?
+	    (asize_before - asize_after) : 0);
+}
+
 /*
  * Determine if the system is under memory pressure and is asking
  * to reclaim memory. A return value of B_TRUE indicates that the system
diff --git a/module/os/osv/zfs/zfs_initialize_osv.c b/module/os/osv/zfs/zfs_initialize_osv.c
--- a/module/os/osv/zfs/zfs_initialize_osv.c
+++ b/module/os/osv/zfs/zfs_initialize_osv.c
@@ -1,1 +1,2 @@
 extern uint64_t arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink(uint64_t to_free);
+extern uint64_t arc_reduce_target_size_shrink_sync(uint64_t to_free);
@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@ osv_arc_lowmem(void *arg, int howto)
 	uint64_t to_free = arc_all_memory() / 4;
 	if (to_free < (16UL << 20))
 		to_free = 16UL << 20;
-	return ((size_t)arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink(to_free));
+	/*
+	 * Hard mode: the reclaimer is about to OOM.  Wait for eviction to
+	 * actually free memory rather than only lowering the target async.
+	 */
+	return ((size_t)arc_reduce_target_size_shrink_sync(to_free));
 }
